.TH DUP 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
dup \- duplicate a file descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int dup(int " descriptor ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Duplicates an open descriptor using the lowest available descriptor number.
The descriptors share the same open file description, including file offset
and status flags. The new descriptor does not have close\-on\-exec set.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the new descriptor, or \-1 with
.B errno
set on failure. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH ERRORS
Include
.BR <errno.h> .
Errors include
.B EBADF
and
.BR EMFILE .
Other Linux dup errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
Crunch errno is process\-wide.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dup2 (3crunch),
.BR close (3crunch),
.BR dup (2)
